   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.4. Number of states in which village council prepare integrated development plans oriented to SDGs.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">None</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Localisation and integration of SDGs at Village Council level to incorporate people living in the last miles
2. SDG localisation through AIR Kohima to incorporate people live in last miles
3. SDG Monitoring Dashboard to monitor the progress of SDG localization in the State
4. SDG Spectrum Newsletter to disseminate activities of SDGCC and raise awareness of people on ongoing SDG localization effort
5. Develop Budget Output-Outcome framework to align the state budget to SDGs 
6. Hornbill festival for leveraging SDG dissemination to the general public 
7. Green Christmas Campaign
8. CSR Matchmaking Platform to promote participation of private sector in achieving SDGs
9. SDG Model District to showcase a replicable model where SDG has been integrated</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Awareness of officials on SDGs at the district, block and village council members increased due to capacity building and dissemination using various tools and channels - including radio, social media, print-media, face-to-face consultations, quarterly newsletter, etc.
2. SDG monitoring dashboard established - monitoring the up-to-date progress of various SDG goals against the indicators. This is helping the government to address critical issues on time.
3. Through the Hornbill Festival 2022, both local and outstations tourists were able to understand get the message of SDGs and the role they can play in contributing to achieving SDGs by 2030 - in the 10-ten event the footfall at the SDG morung exceeded 100,000 - which is a huge achievement.
4. The outcome of the SDG action research projects has been encouraging - as a result five new action research projects has been awarded in 2022.
5. Green Christmas Campaign has been initiated, which is attracting youngsters in huge numbers.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Develop Nagaland SDG Vision document 2030
2. Develop training tool kit- District Manual &#x2013; SDG localization and integration
3. Develop Publicity materials on SDGs
4. Develop SDG Promotional Video
5. Localisation and integration of SDGs at District level
6. Publish second edition of the SDG Spectrum
7. Organise SDG Quiz second series
8. SDG Innovation Participatory Action Research Initiative
9. SDG dissemination through Hornbill Festival and Christmas celebration
10. SDG monitoring dashboard</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Published Nagaland SDG Vision document 2030: Set an ambition/roadmap for the State in order to achieve Agenda 2030.
2. Published training tool kit- District Manual: SDG localization and integration to improve local planning, implementation, monitoring of on-ground programmes
3. Developed Publicity materials on SDGs for awareness generation on SDGs
4. Developed SDG Promotional Video for awareness generation and localization of SDGs
5. Conducted district-level workshop as part of the SDG localization and integration for all 12 districts in the State.
6. Published second edition of SDG Spectrum Newsletter: Knowledge building on the SDGs in a state-specific context.
7. Organised second SDG Quiz series: Generate awareness and knowledge building on SDGs among the residents of Nagaland.
8. SDG Innovation Participatory Action Research Initiative: Mobilize individuals and agencies to take action for the achievement of the priority SDGs and their indicators. There are three ongoing projects under this programme
9. SDG dissemination through Hornbill Festival and Christmas celebration: Greater awareness and encourage on-ground SDG-oriented action as well as align all activities to the SDGs during the Festival period. (ongoing)
10. Developed SDG monitoring dashboard: Enhance monitoring and evaluation at the state and district level. (ongoing)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
